# OpenAPI generated API stub

Spring Framework stub

## Overview
This code was generated by the [OpenAPI Generator](https://openapi-generator.tech) project.
By using the [OpenAPI-Spec](https://openapis.org).
This generates Spring 6+ declarative HTTP interfaces that can be used to easily instantiate an http client.

## Enum arguments

By default, Spring's HTTP interface client sends enum query, path, header, cookie and form arguments using the enum constant name (for example `NAME_COMMA_ASC`), not the value declared in the OpenAPI specification (for example `name,asc`).
The generated `{{configPackage}}.JsonValueEnumToStringConverter` sends the `@JsonValue` value instead. Register it with the `HttpServiceProxyFactory`:

```kotlin
val conversionService = DefaultFormattingConversionService().apply {
    addConverter(JsonValueEnumToStringConverter())
}
val factory = HttpServiceProxyFactory.builderFor(RestClientAdapter.create(restClient))
    .conversionService(conversionService)
    .build()
```

The converter is generic and self-contained. If you generate several clients into one project, you can copy it once into your own code, register that single copy for all clients, and suppress its generation with this ignore rule:

```
**/JsonValueEnumToStringConverter.kt
```

The rule works both in `.openapi-generator-ignore` in the output directory and in a file passed via `--ignore-file-override` (`ignoreFileOverride` in the Maven and Gradle plugins).
Ignore rules are matched relative to the directory containing the ignore file. An exact path such as `{{{jsonValueEnumToStringConverterPath}}}` therefore only matches from `.openapi-generator-ignore` in the output directory.
